theo-pod (t-169): reject an SBR crossover band outside the master table

sbr_reset_dec() derives the high-resolution band count as
Num_Master - xover_band, with xover_band read from the SBR header (3 bits).
When xover_band >= Num_Master the count is zero or negative, and the
low-resolution table is built from FreqBandTable[HI][-1] and below.
ISO/IEC 14496-3 needs at least one high-resolution band; the header is now
rejected with SBRDEC_ILLEGAL_SCFACTORS, as the existing band checks do.
Found by the host fuzzer (UBSan index -2 out of bounds in sbr_reset_dec);
regression input tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sbr-crossover.bin.

